Task complete. Summary:

**Change made** — one line in the `.hud-shell` style block:

````css path=packages/cloudlands-fe/src/routes/hud/+page.svelte mode=EXCERPT
.hud-shell {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  height: 100vh;
  ...
}
````

This sizes the shell against the viewport (matching the `h-screen` convention in `(app)/+layout.svelte`) instead of the unresolvable percentage height, so the footer sits flush with the bottom of the window at any height ≥ 720px. `min-height: 720px` and `min-width: 1280px` are unchanged.

**Verification** (from `packages/cloudlands-fe`):
- `pnpm run check` — 0 errors, 0 warnings
- `pnpm vitest run src/features/hud src/routes/hud` — 22 files, 357 tests, all passed
- No existing test asserts shell sizing (`HudTakeoverOverlay.test.ts` only uses `hud-shell` as a DOM anchor), so no test updates were needed

**One caveat**: the edit is currently uncommitted in the `cloudlands-fe` submodule — `ws.git.commit` operates at the monorepo level and found no changes there. I've noted this in the task note and reported it to the coordinator for the branch/PR flow. Task note is updated and marked complete.
